    "explanation" : "\nEnforces use of `first` instead of `all` with `first` or `[0]`.\n\n# Examples\n\n```ruby\n\n# bad\nall('a').first\nall('a')[0]\nfind('a', match: :first)\nall('a', match: :first)\n\n# good\nfirst('a')\n```\n\n[Source](http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/rubocop/RuboCop/Cop/Capybara/FindAllFirst)",
