    "description" : "This rule checks for the usage of deprecated Capybara style assertion methods and enforces the use of their updated equivalents.",
    "explanation" : "\nChecks for usage of deprecated style methods.\n\n# Examples\n\n```ruby\n# bad\npage.find(:css, '#first').assert_style(display: 'block')\n\n# good\npage.find(:css, '#first').assert_matches_style(display: 'block')# bad\nexpect(page.find(:css, 'first')\n  .has_style?(display: 'block')).to be true\n\n# good\nexpect(page.find(:css, 'first')\n  .matches_style?(display: 'block')).to be true# bad\nexpect(page).to have_style(display: 'block')\n\n# good\nexpect(page).to match_style(display: 'block')\n```\n\n[Source](http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/rubocop/RuboCop/Cop/Capybara/MatchStyle)",
