    "explanation" : "\nChecks for a line break before the first parameter in a\nmulti-line method parameter definition.\n\n# Examples\n\n```ruby\n\n# bad\ndef method(foo, bar,\n    baz)\n  do_something\nend\n\n# good\ndef method(\n    foo, bar,\n    baz)\n  do_something\nend\n\n# ignored\ndef method foo,\n    bar\n  do_something\nend\n# bad\ndef method(foo, bar, baz = {\n  :a => \"b\",\n})\n  do_something\nend\n\n# good\ndef method(\n  foo, bar, baz = {\n  :a => \"b\",\n})\n  do_something\nend\n# good\ndef method(foo, bar, baz = {\n  :a => \"b\",\n})\n  do_something\nend\n```\n\n[Source](http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/rubocop/RuboCop/Cop/Layout/FirstMethodParameterLineBreak)",
