    "explanation" : "\nChecks the indentation of the method name part in method calls\nthat span more than one line.\n\n# Examples\n\n```ruby\n# bad\nwhile myvariable\n.b\n  # do something\nend\n\n# good\nwhile myvariable\n      .b\n  # do something\nend\n\n# good\nThing.a\n     .b\n     .c# good\nwhile myvariable\n  .b\n\n  # do something\nend# good\nwhile myvariable\n        .a\n        .b\n\n  # do something\nend\n\n# good\nmyvariable = Thing\n               .a\n               .b\n               .c\n```\n\n[Source](http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/rubocop/RuboCop/Cop/Layout/MultilineMethodCallIndentation)",
