    "id" : "Lint_NoReturnInBeginEndBlocks",
    "level" : "High",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid return inside begin..end blocks in assignment contexts",
    "description" : "This rule checks for the use of return statements inside begin..end blocks when used in assignment contexts, which can cause unexpected method exits.",
    "explanation" : "\nChecks for the presence of a `return` inside a `begin..end` block\nin assignment contexts.\nIn this situation, the `return` will result in an exit from the current\nmethod, possibly leading to unexpected behavior.\n\n# Examples\n\n```ruby\n\n# bad\n@some_variable ||= begin\n  return some_value if some_condition_is_met\n\n  do_something\nend\n\n# good\n@some_variable ||= begin\n  if some_condition_is_met\n    some_value\n  else\n    do_something\n  end\nend\n\n# good\nsome_variable = if some_condition_is_met\n                  return if another_condition_is_met\n\n                  some_value\n                else\n                  do_something\n                end\n```\n\n[Source](http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/rubocop/RuboCop/Cop/Lint/NoReturnInBeginEndBlocks)",
