    "id" : "Packaging_GemspecGit",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Using Git Commands in Gemspec Files",
    "description" : "This rule flags the usage of git commands like `git ls-files` in gemspec files and recommends using plain Ruby alternatives for specifying files.",
    "explanation" : "\nThis cop flags the usage of `git ls-files` in gemspec\nand suggests to use a plain Ruby alternative, like `Dir`,\n`Dir.glob`, or `Rake::FileList` instead.\n\n# Examples\n\n```ruby\n\n# bad\nGem::Specification.new do |spec|\n  spec.files = `git ls-files`.split(\"\\n\")\nend\n\n# good\nGem::Specification.new do |spec|\n  spec.files = Dir[\"lib/**/*\", \"LICENSE\", \"README.md\"]\nend\n\n# bad\nGem::Specification.new do |spec|\n  spec.files = Dir.chdir(File.expand_path(__dir__)) do\n    `git ls-files -z`.split(\"\\\\x0\").reject { |f| f.match(%r{^(test|spec|features)/}) }\n  end\nend\n\n# good\nrequire \"rake/file_list\"\n\nGem::Specification.new do |spec|\n  spec.files = Rake::FileList[\"**/*\"].exclude(*File.read(\".gitignore\").split)\nend\n\n# bad\nGem::Specification.new do |spec|\n  spec.files        = `git ls-files -- lib/`.split(\"\\n\")\n  spec.executables  = `git ls-files -- bin/*`.split(\"\\n\").map{ |f| File.basename(f) }\nend\n\n# good\nGem::Specification.new do |spec|\n  spec.files        = Dir.glob(\"lib/**/*\")\n  spec.executables  = Dir.glob(\"bin/*\").map{ |f| File.basename(f) }\nend\n```\n\n[Source](http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/rubocop/RuboCop/Cop/Packaging/GemspecGit)",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
