    "description" : "Enforces the use of Ruby's safe navigation operator (&.) instead of try! for method calls.",
    "explanation" : "\nConverts usages of `try!` to `&.`. It can also be configured\nto convert `try`. It will convert code to use safe navigation\nif the target Ruby version is set to 2.3+\n\n# Examples\n\n```ruby\n# bad\nfoo.try!(:bar)\nfoo.try!(:bar, baz)\nfoo.try!(:bar) { |e| e.baz }\n\nfoo.try!(:[], 0)\n\n# good\nfoo.try(:bar)\nfoo.try(:bar, baz)\nfoo.try(:bar) { |e| e.baz }\n\nfoo&.bar\nfoo&.bar(baz)\nfoo&.bar { |e| e.baz }# bad\nfoo.try!(:bar)\nfoo.try!(:bar, baz)\nfoo.try!(:bar) { |e| e.baz }\nfoo.try(:bar)\nfoo.try(:bar, baz)\nfoo.try(:bar) { |e| e.baz }\n\n# good\nfoo&.bar\nfoo&.bar(baz)\nfoo&.bar { |e| e.baz }\n```\n\n[Source](http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/rubocop/RuboCop/Cop/Rails/SafeNavigation)",
