    "explanation" : "\nChecks for grouping of accessors in `class` and `module` bodies.\nBy default it enforces accessors to be placed in grouped declarations,\nbut it can be configured to enforce separating them in multiple declarations.\n\nNOTE: If there is a method call before the accessor method it is always allowed\nas it might be intended like Sorbet.\n\nNOTE: If there is a RBS::Inline annotation comment just after the accessor method\nit is always allowed.\n\n# Examples\n\n```ruby\n# bad\nclass Foo\n  attr_reader :bar\n  attr_reader :bax\n  attr_reader :baz\nend\n\n# good\nclass Foo\n  attr_reader :bar, :bax, :baz\nend\n\n# good\nclass Foo\n  # may be intended comment for bar.\n  attr_reader :bar\n\n  sig { returns(String) }\n  attr_reader :bax\n\n  may_be_intended_annotation :baz\n  attr_reader :baz\nend# bad\nclass Foo\n  attr_reader :bar, :baz\nend\n\n# good\nclass Foo\n  attr_reader :bar\n  attr_reader :baz\nend\n```\n\n[Source](http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/rubocop/RuboCop/Cop/Style/AccessorGrouping)",
