    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Prefer case-when over if-elsif for multiple conditions",
    "description" : "Detects if-elsif constructions that can be more clearly expressed using case-when statements.",
    "explanation" : "\nIdentifies places where `if-elsif` constructions\ncan be replaced with `case-when`.\n\n# Examples\n\n```ruby\n# bad\nif status == :active\n  perform_action\nelsif status == :inactive || status == :hibernating\n  check_timeout\nelsif status == :invalid\n  report_invalid\nelse\n  final_action\nend\n\n# good\ncase status\nwhen :active\n  perform_action\nwhen :inactive, :hibernating\n  check_timeout\nwhen :invalid\n  report_invalid\nelse\n  final_action\nend# good\nif status == :active\n  perform_action\nelsif status == :inactive || status == :hibernating\n  check_timeout\nelsif status == :invalid\n  report_invalid\nelse\n  final_action\nend\n```\n\n[Source](http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/rubocop/RuboCop/Cop/Style/CaseLikeIf)",
