    "title" : "Favor File.read and File.binread Convenience Methods",
    "description" : "This rule encourages the use of File.read and File.binread convenience methods instead of opening a file and then reading it.",
    "explanation" : "\nFavor `File.(bin)read` convenience methods.\n\n# Examples\n\n```ruby\n# bad - text mode\nFile.open(filename).read\nFile.open(filename, &:read)\nFile.open(filename) { |f| f.read }\nFile.open(filename) do |f|\n  f.read\nend\nFile.open(filename, 'r').read\nFile.open(filename, 'r', &:read)\nFile.open(filename, 'r') do |f|\n  f.read\nend\n\n# good\nFile.read(filename)\n\n# bad - binary mode\nFile.open(filename, 'rb').read\nFile.open(filename, 'rb', &:read)\nFile.open(filename, 'rb') do |f|\n  f.read\nend\n\n# good\nFile.binread(filename)\n```\n\n[Source](http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/rubocop/RuboCop/Cop/Style/FileRead)",
