    "id" : "Style_RedundantFilterChain",
    "level" : "Info",
    "category" : "Performance",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Redundant Predicate Method Chains After Filter Methods",
    "description" : "Detects and replaces redundant uses of predicate methods like any?, empty?, none?, or one? chained after select/filter/find_all with the more efficient predicate method form.",
    "explanation" : "\nIdentifies usages of `any?`, `empty?` or `none?` predicate methods\nchained to `select`/`filter`/`find_all` and change them to use predicate method instead.\n\n# Examples\n\n```ruby\n# bad\narr.select { |x| x > 1 }.any?\n\n# good\narr.any? { |x| x > 1 }\n\n# bad\narr.select { |x| x > 1 }.empty?\narr.select { |x| x > 1 }.none?\n\n# good\narr.none? { |x| x > 1 }\n\n# good\nrelation.select(:name).any?\narr.select { |x| x > 1 }.any?(&:odd?)# good\narr.select { |x| x > 1 }.many?\n\n# good\narr.select { |x| x > 1 }.present?# bad\narr.select { |x| x > 1 }.many?\n\n# good\narr.many? { |x| x > 1 }\n\n# bad\narr.select { |x| x > 1 }.present?\n\n# good\narr.any? { |x| x > 1 }\n```\n\n[Source](http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/rubocop/RuboCop/Cop/Style/RedundantFilterChain)",
