    "description" : "Checks for and disallows unnecessary use of return statements where the return is implied.",
    "explanation" : "\nChecks for redundant `return` expressions.\n\n# Examples\n\n```ruby\n# These bad cases should be extended to handle methods whose body is\n# if/else or a case expression with a default branch.\n\n# bad\ndef test\n  return something\nend\n\n# bad\ndef test\n  one\n  two\n  three\n  return something\nend\n\n# bad\ndef test\n  return something if something_else\nend\n\n# good\ndef test\n  something if something_else\nend\n\n# good\ndef test\n  if x\n  elsif y\n  else\n  end\nend# bad\ndef test\n  return x, y\nend# good\ndef test\n  return x, y\nend\n```\n\n[Source](http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/rubocop/RuboCop/Cop/Style/RedundantReturn)",
