    "explanation" : "\nIf the branch of a conditional consists solely of a conditional node,\nits conditions can be combined with the conditions of the outer branch.\nThis helps to keep the nesting level from getting too deep.\n\n# Examples\n\n```ruby\n# bad\nif condition_a\n  if condition_b\n    do_something\n  end\nend\n\n# bad\nif condition_b\n  do_something\nend if condition_a\n\n# good\nif condition_a && condition_b\n  do_something\nend# bad\nif condition_a\n  do_something if condition_b\nend\n\n# bad\nif condition_b\n  do_something\nend if condition_a# good\nif condition_a\n  do_something if condition_b\nend\n\n# good\nif condition_b\n  do_something\nend if condition_a\n```\n\n[Source](http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/rubocop/RuboCop/Cop/Style/SoleNestedConditional)",
